  "body": "## Bug\n\nThe `camcraft-ui` GPU integration test process exited with SIGSEGV after several tests passed. Each test creates and drops its own fallback wgpu device, and Rust runs the tests concurrently. Overlapping device lifecycles appear to trigger a software Vulkan driver crash.\n\n## Fix\n\nSerialize device creation, rendering, readback, and teardown within `gpu_render.rs` using a test-only mutex. Other test binaries and application rendering are unchanged.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Before the fix: `cargo test --locked -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui` reached `gpu_render.rs`, then exited with SIGSEGV after five GPU tests passed.\n- After the fix: all nine `gpu_render` tests passed, followed by the full `camcraft-app` and `camcraft-ui` test run on Fedora 44.\n\nChangelog: Prevent concurrent GPU test devices from crashing the render test suite.\n",
